# Jetson deploy (git only)

When deploying to the Jetson edge device (`172.16.90.20`, repo at `/var/projects/agentic-orchestration`):

## Required workflow

1. **Commit and push** all changes to `main` on the `github` remote (local dev machine).
2. **On the Jetson**, update only from git — never `scp`, never copy files by hand:
   ```bash
   cd /var/projects/agentic-orchestration
   git fetch origin
   git pull origin main
   bash agentic-orchestration-tool/scripts/jetson-deploy.sh
   ```
   Or use the all-in-one script after pull:
   ```bash
   bash agentic-orchestration-tool/scripts/jetson-deploy.sh
   ```
   (`jetson-deploy.sh` runs `git pull` then env sync + hotfix.)

3. If coordinator rollout stalls on hostPort 80, scale the **old** coordinator ReplicaSet to 0:
   ```bash
   export KUBECONFIG=/etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml
   kubectl get rs -n agentic-orchestration | grep coordinator
   kubectl scale rs <old-rs-name> -n agentic-orchestration --replicas=0
   kubectl rollout status deployment/agentic-coordinator -n agentic-orchestration --timeout=120s
   ```

## Forbidden

- `scp` files to the Jetson
- Editing tracked files on the Jetson without committing to git first
- Deploying from uncommitted local-only changes

## Jetson git remote

The device uses remote **`origin`** (not `github`). Push from dev with `git push github main`; pull on Jetson with `git pull origin main`.

## Scripts (run on Jetson after git pull)

| Script | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `jetson-deploy.sh` | Routine deploy: pull + apply-env + sync-k8s-secret + hotfix-web |
| `jetson-apply-env.sh` | Merge `config/env.jetson` → `.env` |
| `jetson-sync-k8s-secret.sh` | Refresh k8s secret + restart coordinator/warm-pool |
| `jetson-hotfix-web.sh` | ConfigMap hotfix for web + orchestration Python |

Full stack rebuild (rare): `sudo bash scripts/jetson-k3s-deploy.sh` (also git-pulls first).
